From: RK3128 reference <reference@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: clear RK3128 shared block state after TRNG use

Close each TRNG transaction with the vendor hiword clear and acknowledge
oscillator disable before releasing the shared lock. Withhold startup bits
on every restart while preserving continuous health history. Retain live
resources and refuse all access after an unacknowledged close/stop.
Clear shared block FIFO/FSM state with the documented timed flush, also
selectively keeping cipher DMA disabled in the shipping hash/PIO profile.

Signed-off-by: RK3128 reference <reference@example.invalid>

diff --git a/drivers/crypto/Kconfig b/drivers/crypto/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/crypto/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/crypto/Kconfig
@@ -700,6 +700,15 @@
 	  Uses private coherent DMA buffers, bounded hardware deadlines and
 	  a serialized crypto engine. Streaming hashes use software fallback.
 
+config CRYPTO_DEV_RK3128_HASH_PIO
+	bool "Restrict RK3128 ciphers to low-priority PIO"
+	depends on CRYPTO_DEV_RK3128
+	help
+	  Keep MD5/SHA1/SHA256 DMA and the health-tested oscillator, but
+	  reject cipher DMA. AES/DES/3DES wrappers use the accepted PIO
+	  primitive at priority 1, below CPU implementations. Diagnostic
+	  parameters cannot enable cipher DMA in this configuration.
+
 config CRYPTO_DEV_ROCKCHIP_DEBUG
 	bool "Enable Rockchip crypto stats"
 	depends on CRYPTO_DEV_ROCKCHIP
